":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"global-panel-open-state-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find hover/click/dirty global panels whose open state is a boolean, then replace them with explicit open reasons, pinned state, delayed-close ownership, and keyboard/touch semantics."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inline-svg-duplicate-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find unreferenced or near-duplicate inline SVG logo/icon components, fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clipPath"},{"type":"text","value":" collisions, and candidates for static assets or one typed wrapper."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"product-landing-shell-extractor"},{"type":"text","value":": find repeated product landing imports, hero CTA shapes, download proof, prompt-copy controls, sponsor/community/footer tails, and demo lifecycle rules, then extract only the stable page shell contract."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"product-card-interaction-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find listing cards that combine card-level click/keyboard handlers with nested buttons, links, swatches, or eager hover-media preloads, then split interactions and add preload budgets."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"repeated-form-control-id-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find repeated table rows, field arrays, dialogs, or expanded panels that render fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"htmlFor"},{"type":"text","value":" pairs, then derive stable row-local ids."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client-response-schema-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find client fetch helpers that cast JSON to application types while the server only validates requests, then add shared response schemas and typed error envelopes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"frontmatter-parse-resilience-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find docs/content loaders where one malformed frontmatter block can break manifests, pages, or global indexes, then add typed parse results and skip/report behavior."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial-cache-hit-contract-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find chunked cache readers that return partial data as if it were complete, then split full-hit, partial-hit, stale-hit, and miss semantics."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"programmatic-window-open-helper-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.open"},{"type":"text","value":" callsites and normalize "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"noopener,noreferrer"},{"type":"text","value":", blocked-popup handling, fallback anchors, and user-gesture expectations."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tarball-path-normalization-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find package tarball paths stored or rendered as source URLs, then normalize path segments and block traversal/encoding edge cases."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state-machine-final-transition-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find XState/state-machine guards that test completion before assignment actions, then add final-item regression tests for each phase."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"landing-demo-dogfooding-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": compare product landing demos against the actual product APIs they describe, then classify each demo as intentional mock, static illustration, or API-backed example with lazy-loading and cleanup policy."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"route-link-helper-type-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find local "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Link"},{"type":"text","value":" wrappers that accept "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"to: string"},{"type":"text","value":", loose params, or secondary-link route strings, then replace them with typed route helpers or one typed CTA primitive."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"public-preview-bundle-query-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find marketing pages that mount registry/stats/chart previews on initial render, then decide which should be static, viewport-gated, or lazy-loaded behind interaction."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"game-engine-lifecycle-and-vector-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": review Three.js game code for shared geometry ownership, async loader cancellation, timer cleanup, zero-distance vector math, and duplicate active/dead scene stacks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"directory-view-mode-component-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find public directory pages that copy segmented view controls, card grid switches, and animation wrappers, then extract a typed reusable controller without coupling route filters together."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auth-scoped-query-cache-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find current-user/private React Query keys that omit user/session fingerprints, then add scoped keys and auth transition cache clearing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"analytics-cardinality-privacy-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find analytics props that carry raw UUIDs, random seeds, user-entered strings, URLs, or other high-cardinality identifiers, then replace them with bounded cohorts, versions, and explicit debug-only channels."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"admin-capability-contract-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": compare admin nav items, route "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" guards, client guard components, and server-function capability checks so partial moderators never see or trigger admin-only surfaces."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"capability-boundary-validation-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find server functions, loaders, and client helpers that cast capability strings instead of validating against the shared capability registry."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"doc-feedback-scale-contract-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": cap feedback content/selectors/pagination, move leaderboard aggregation out of all-table JS reads, and extract one cache-update helper for feedback envelopes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"worker-background-task-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find fire-and-forget promises inside request handlers, then convert them to awaited work, queues, or runtime background-task primitives."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessible-table-disclosure-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find clickable table headers/rows that rely on pointer interaction and replace them with native buttons, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-sort"},{"type":"text","value":", and disclosure semantics."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"admin-keyed-row-action-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": find table/list actions whose mutation state disables every row, then replace them with keyed pending/error state and per-row double-click guards."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"route-font-asset-audit"},{"type":"text","value":": compare route "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<link>"},{"type":"text","value":" font loads, CSS "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@import"},{"type":"text","value":"s, and Tailwind font tokens to remove duplicate families, unused families, and mismatched mono/display tokens."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"suggested-next-passes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suggested Next Passes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Triage the P0/P1/P2 findings into small fix PRs, starting with auth/OAuth, analytics proxy headers, builder endpoint guards, stats fan-out caps, and Shopify/search validation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ANALYZE=1 pnpm build"},{"type":"text","value":" only when ready to pay the build cost, then compare actual chunks against the bundle findings above."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add focused tests for the high-risk fixes before changing auth/token, builder, stats, Intent ingestion, markdown, and Shopify behavior."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add a reachability/dead-code pass to the regular workflow so unused SVG, R3F, shop promo, and global CSS utility code does not grow back."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tests","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tests"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No tests were run for this report. This pass made no application code changes."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"source-code-audit-2026-06-23","text":"Source Code Audit - 2026-06-23","level":1},{"id":"merged-fix-order","text":"Merged Fix Order","level":2},{"id":"1-small-shared-guardrails","text":"1. Small shared guardrails","level":3},{"id":"2-one-off-cleanup-that-lowers-noise","text":"2. One-off cleanup that lowers noise","level":3},{"id":"3-fast-security-and-public-boundary-hardening","text":"3. Fast security and public-boundary hardening","level":3},{"id":"4-small-controllers-that-prevent-repeat-bugs","text":"4. Small controllers that prevent repeat bugs","level":3},{"id":"5-domain-hardening-with-shared-primitives-in-place","text":"5. Domain hardening with shared primitives in place","level":3},{"id":"6-larger-boundary-refactors","text":"6. Larger boundary refactors","level":3},{"id":"7-product-wide-initiatives-and-upstream-candidates","text":"7. Product-wide initiatives and upstream candidates","level":3},{"id":"batch-log","text":"Batch Log","level":2},{"id":"highest-priority-findings","text":"Highest Priority Findings","level":2},{"id":"p0-p1-analytics-proxy-forwards-private-request-headers","text":"P0/P1 - Analytics proxy forwards private request headers","level":3},{"id":"p1-oauth-authorization-codes-are-not-consumed-atomically","text":"P1 - OAuth authorization codes are not consumed atomically","level":3},{"id":"p1-oauth-client-ids-are-not-bound-to-registered-redirect-uris","text":"P1 - OAuth client IDs are not bound to registered redirect URIs","level":3},{"id":"p1-client-ip-extraction-trusts-spoofable-headers-before-cloudflare","text":"P1 - Client IP extraction trusts spoofable headers before Cloudflare","level":3},{"id":"p1-public-npm-stats-requests-can-cause-unbounded-fan-out","text":"P1 - Public npm stats requests can cause unbounded fan-out","level":3},{"id":"p2-npm-stats-ui-search-state-is-unbounded-too","text":"P2 - NPM stats UI search state is unbounded too","le